  "chapter": {
    "number": 115,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(116) Alleluia."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I am well pleased, because the Lord will listen to the voice of my supplication.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Because he has inclined his ear to me, therefore will I call upon him while I live.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The pangs of death compassed me; the dangers of hell found me: I found affliction and sorrow.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Then I called on the name of the Lord: O Lord, deliver my soul.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord is merciful and righteous; yes, our God has pity.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord preserves",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 216
          },
          {
            "text": "the simple: I was brought low, and he delivered me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Return to your rest, O my soul; for the Lord has dealt bountifully with you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For he has delivered my soul from death, my eyes from tears, and my feet from falling.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I shall be well-pleasing before the Lord in the land of the living.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "text": "(115) Alleluia.",
            "descriptive": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "noteId": 217
          },
          {
            "text": "I believed, therefore I have spoken: but I was greatly afflicted.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And I said in my amazement, Every man is a liar.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "What shall I render to the Lord for all the things wherein he has rewarded me?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will take the cup of salvation, and call upon the name of the Lord.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will pay my vows to the Lord, in the presence of all his people.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Precious in the sight of the Lord is the death of his saints.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O Lord, I am your servant; I am your servant, and the son of your handmaid: you have burst my bonds asunder.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will offer to you the sacrifice of praise, and will call upon the name of the Lord.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 18,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will pay my vows to the Lord, in the presence of all his people,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 19,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "in the courts of the Lord's house, in the midst of you, Jerusalem.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
